# Quest authoring entry point

Read agents/README.md, _registry/QUESTLINE_CONTENT_RULES.md and _registry/MINIGAME_TEACHING_GUIDE.md before designing or editing learning content. Use the Designer -> Creator -> QA cycle and agents/BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md. These shared files own policy; this file routes to them.

- Work within the user's scope and current checkout. Do not require repeated approval for authorized routine decisions.
- The current catalog has eight games; recheck _registry/minigames.yaml rather than relying on a fixed historical count.
- Use exact IDs from systems.yaml, npcs.yaml, areas.yaml, interactables.yaml, items.yaml and softkitty_items.yaml. Prefer live_used stations; consult catalog pictures for setting.
- New questline topics are allowed when requested; there is no four-line allowlist. Do not restore deleted content without a request.
- Authorized new story characters are proposals/off-screen figures until a registered speaker exists. Do not invent technical IDs or runtime capabilities.
- Read relevant quests for continuity/prerequisites. Use catalog/YAML IDs, not names copied from a presentation.
- Use globally unique line-scoped keys, update index/prerequisites/rewards/graph, and keep current turn-in conventions.
- No reach_location unless requested; no trailing return_to_npc or duplicate closing talk step.
- Learner-facing Hebrew is simple and without niqqud by default. Dialogue and minigame instructions have distinct purposes.
- Letter Drawing uses one manual symbols list, each entry a letter or a whole word.
- Listen & Build is listening_letter_ordering and requires real matching audio for a listening objective.
- Follow the current Speak Aloud display contract; do not assume one-word targetWords preserves a full targetPhrase on screen.
- For hosted import, use the single procedure in agents/README.md. Report draft/published status and verification honestly.
